  "raw_text": "256\n\nTingkikira\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \nthankful, grateful\n, appreciative\n \n/ agradecido\n, apreciativo\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nTingkikira bas.\n \n–\n \nBe appreciative.\n \n/ S\né\n \napreciativo.; Sea apreciativo.\n)\n\nTingni\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncreek, stream, brook\n \n/ arroyo\n\nTingting\n \n(\ndict,dictu\n;\n \nTinhting\n-\ndictu-alt\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nelbow\n \n/ codo\n\nTininis\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nhummingbird\n \n/ colibrí\n\nTint watla\n \n(a/t:\n \nTent watla\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ntent\n \n/ tienda\n\nGâd tintka watla\n \n(\nlfb25\n;\n \nGâd tentka\n-\nmy\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \n(God’s) tabernacle, (God’s) tent\n \n/ tabernáculo (de Dios), tienda\n(de Dios)\n \n(see/ver:\n \nmy37\n;\n \ndb\n \nusually refers to the tabernacle as\n \nUtla\n \nor\n \nWatla\n \n/\n \ndb\n \ngeneralmente se refiere al\ntabernáculo como\n \nUtla\n \no\n \nWatla\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nlfb25\n):\n \nGâd tintka watla ba sip kan brih waia\n \n–\n \nGod’s tabernacle was able to be carried\n \n/ El tabernáculo de Dios\n\npudo ser llevado\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n11/20\n):\n \nG\nȃ\nd tintka watla paskaia warkka tnata aimakan taim, Moses mita warkka ba laki kaikan.\n \n–\n \nWhen the\n\nwork to make God’s tabernacle was completed, the work was examined by Moses.\n \n/\n \nCuando se completó la obra para\n\nhacer el tabernáculo de Dios,\n \nel trabajo fue examinado por Moisés.\n)\n\nTint watla dusa\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ntent p\neg\n \n/ clavija de tienda\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nlfb32\n):\n \nJael ... tint watla dusa tatwa kum wal lal ra saban, bara witin pruan\n \n–\n \nJael ... stabbed (him) in the head with\n\na pointy tent peg, and he died\n \n/ Jael ... lo apuñaló en la cabeza con una clavija puntiaguda y murió\n)\n\nTips\n \n(\ndb\n,\ndictu-alt\n;\n \nTeps\n-\ndictu\n,\ndict\n;\n \nStep\n-\ndictu\n,\ndict\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nsteps, stairs\n \n/ escalones, escaleras\n\nTisbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto press, to squeeze, to tighten, to trample\n \n/ apretar, presionar, pisotear\n\nTisbaika dusa\n \n–\n \nstick used to tamper the ground\n \n/ palo para pisar\n \no apelmazar\n \nel suelo\n \n(como un pis\nó\nn)\n\nTisku\n \n(adj,adv)\n \n–\n \nsoon\n \n/ pronto\n\n(Note/Nota: sometimes used to say “see you soon”\n/ a veces solía decir \"hasta pronto\n”\n)\n\nTisku pali\n \n–\n \nvery soon\n \n/ muy pronto\n\nTisku ra\n \n–\n \nin a little while, later on\n \n/ en poco tiempo, luego\n\nTit\n \n(a/t:\n \nTitit, Titik\n) (Onomatopoeia / Onomatopeya)\n \n–\n \nthis onomatopoeia adds the idea of:\n \ninstantly, suddenly\n \n/ esta\nonomatopeya agrega la idea de: instantáneamente, de repente\n\nTit buaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto rise instantly, to rise suddenly, to stand up instantly, to stand up suddenly\n \n/ levantarse al\ninstante, levantarse de repente, ponerse de pie al instante, ponerse de pie de repente\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Aiseya 48:3\n):\n \nTit bui daukri bara baku dukia nani ba pain takan.\n \n–\n \nnwt\n:\n \nSuddenly I took action, and they came\nabout.\n \n/\n \ntnm\n: De repente actué, y se realizaron.\n)\n\nTitan\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nmorning\n \n/ mañana\n\nTitan mayunra\n \n–\n \nmorning worship\n \n/ adoración matutina\n\nTitan pali\n \n–\n \nearly in the morning\n \n/ temprano en la mañana\n\nTitan pata\n \n–\n \nbreakfast\n \n/ desayuno\n\nTitan puk\n \n–\n \nearly in the morning\n \n/ temprano en la mañana\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-2 Kronikas 29:20\n):\n \nKing Ezequías ba titan puk ba ra buan\n \n–\n \nKing Hezekiah got up early in the morning\n \n/ El rey\nEzequías se levantó temprano en la mañana)\n\nTitan tanira\n \n–\n \nin the morning\n \n/ por la mañana\n\nTitan yamni\n \n(a greeting / un saludo)\n \n–\n \nGood morning\n \n/ Buenos días\n\nTitikbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto rub, to scrub, to scratch, to grind, to tear something apart\n \n/ restregar, rascar, triturar, despedazar una\ncosa\n\nTitikbi ikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto kill all completely, to exterminate\n \n/ matar a todos por completo, exterminar\n\nTiun\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ntune, melody\n \n/ melodía\n\nTiusdi\n \n(\ndictu,km\n;\n \nTiusde\n,\nSusde\n-\ndict\n;\n \nSusdi\n-\nmy\n;\n \nTiusde\n–\ndictu-alt\n)\n \n–\n \nTuesday\n \n/ martes\n\nTiwaia\n \n(v-intrans; trans:\n \nTikaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto be lost, to disappear, to go astray, to dissipate\n \n/ estar perdido, desaparecer,\nextraviarse, disiparse\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nvi\n):\n \nLuki kaiks man tiwram sa\n \n–\n \nImagine you are lost\n \n/ Imagina que estás perdido)\n\nAuya tiwaia\n \n(v-intrans; trans:\n \nAuya tikaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto forget, to lose the memory\n \n/ olvidar, perder la memoria\n\nAmya tiwbiara\n \n(v-neg-f)\n \n–\n \nnot to forget, do not forget, we are not to forget, one is not to forget, we must\nnot forget, one must not forget\n \n/ no olvidar, no debemos olvidar, uno no debe olvidar\n\nAuya tiwan\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nhe/she forg\ne\nt\ns\n \n/ él/ella olvid\na\n\n(Lit: The memory is lost / La memoria está perdida)",
